{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1561366055,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0NTk3NjY5MDg=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3487","origin":"github"},"title":"Q: Trajectory to make SSHConnection more useful","message":"I am using this functionality more and more, but it is rather clunky. For example, it is not easy to stream large outputs (think decompressing a remote archive and storing the output locally without making tmp copies, etc.\n\nI see two paths forward:\n\n1. Expose internal pieces, such as SSH command generation, so that could be used with an outside \"runner\".\n2. Add a dedicated `.run()` that sits on top of `subprocess.run()` and takes the same args.\n\nThe later is PY3.5+ only, so we likely don't want to base internal functionality on it, but it would be very helpful in order to have the entire range of possibilities available via a standard interface, plus the connection handling functionality that we provide.\n\nWhat do you think?","files":null}]}